Build a professional full-stack web app called **Smart Attendance System** for managing student attendance using unique QR codes.

### 1. Student Registration / First-Time Login

When a student opens the app for the first time, show a registration/login screen.

Required fields:

* Student Name
* Roll Number
* Phone Number
* Email ID (optional)
* Course / Branch
* Semester / Section

After registration:

* Save the student's information permanently in the database.
* Generate a unique Student ID.
* Generate a unique QR code linked to that student's ID.
* The QR code should remain the same for that student unless the teacher/admin resets it.
* Do not allow two students to register with the same Roll Number.
* Student should be able to log in later using their registered phone number/roll number.

### 2. Student Dashboard

After login, show a clean dashboard containing:

* Student Name
* Roll Number
* Course / Branch
* Semester / Section
* Student's unique QR code
* Total Classes
* Classes Attended
* Attendance Percentage
* Recent attendance records

Add a prominent **"My QR Code"** section so the student can easily display their QR code to the scanner.

### 3. Attendance Scanning

Create a teacher/admin attendance scanner.

Teacher should be able to:

* Select Class / Subject
* Start an attendance session
* Scan the student's QR code using the device camera
* Automatically identify the student
* Mark the student as PRESENT
* Save:

  * Student Name
  * Roll Number
  * Subject
  * Date
  * Exact attendance time
  * Attendance status
  * Class/session ID

After successful scanning show:
**"Attendance Marked Successfully"**

Also display the student's name and roll number after scanning so the teacher can verify the correct student.

### 4. Duplicate Attendance Protection

A student must not be able to mark attendance twice for the same class/session.

If the same QR code is scanned again during the same session, show:
**"Attendance Already Marked"**

Do not create duplicate attendance records.

### 5. Classroom Security / Proxy Prevention

Add an optional **Classroom Verification** feature to reduce proxy attendance.

When the teacher starts an attendance session:

* Generate a temporary attendance session.
* Only QR scans during the active session should be accepted.
* Session should automatically expire after the teacher ends the class.
* Store the classroom/session information with every attendance record.

Also add an optional **classroom QR / session QR** verification layer where students must first scan the classroom QR and then show their personal QR.

The system should clearly separate:

* Student QR
* Classroom/session QR

This should make it harder for students outside the classroom to submit attendance.

### 6. Teacher Dashboard

Create a professional teacher dashboard with:

**Dashboard statistics**

* Total Students
* Present Today
* Absent Today
* Attendance Percentage
* Active Attendance Session

**Student Management**

* Add Student
* Edit Student
* Delete/Deactivate Student
* Search by Name
* Search by Roll Number
* View Student QR

**Attendance Management**

* Start Attendance Session
* Scan QR
* View Today's Attendance
* View attendance by date
* View attendance by subject
* View attendance by student
* Manually correct attendance if required

### 7. Attendance History

Create a complete attendance history page.

Each record should show:

* Date
* Time
* Student Name
* Roll Number
* Subject
* Class/Section
* Status: Present/Absent
* Attendance session

Add filters:

* Date
* Student
* Roll Number
* Subject
* Section
* Attendance status

### 8. Attendance Percentage

Automatically calculate each student's attendance percentage:

Attendance Percentage =
(Present Classes / Total Classes) × 100

Show the percentage clearly on the student dashboard and teacher dashboard.

Use visual indicators for:

* Good attendance
* Low attendance
* Critical attendance

### 9. Reports

Add a Reports section where teachers can:

* Generate daily attendance report
* Generate monthly attendance report
* Generate student-wise report
* Generate subject-wise report
* Export attendance as CSV
* Export attendance as Excel/PDF if supported

### 10. Authentication & Roles

Create two roles:

**Student**

* Login
* View profile
* View personal QR
* View attendance history
* View attendance percentage

**Teacher/Admin**

* Secure login
* Manage students
* Create classes/subjects
* Start attendance sessions
* Scan QR codes
* View and manage attendance
* Generate reports

Students must not be able to access teacher/admin pages.

### 11. Database

Create a proper relational database with tables/collections for:

* Users
* Students
* Teachers
* Subjects
* Classes/Sections
* Attendance Sessions
* Attendance Records

Use proper relationships and unique constraints.

Important:

* Roll Number must be unique within the appropriate class/section.
* Student QR ID must be unique.
* Attendance should have a unique constraint for Student + Attendance Session to prevent duplicates.

### 12. UI/UX

Make the application look like a modern professional college attendance management system.

Use:

* Responsive design
* Clean dashboard
* Sidebar navigation
* Cards for statistics
* Tables for attendance
* Search and filter controls
* QR scanner interface
* Mobile-friendly student dashboard
* Professional typography
* Clear success/error notifications

Create separate navigation for Student and Teacher/Admin.

### 13. Important User Flow

Student flow:

Register → Enter Name/Roll No./Phone → Save Student Data → Generate Unique QR → Student Dashboard → Show Personal QR → Teacher Scans QR → Attendance Marked → Attendance History Updated

Teacher flow:

Login → Select Class/Subject → Start Attendance Session → Scan Student QR → Verify Student → Mark Present → Save Date & Time → Continue Scanning → End Session

### 14. Extra Features

Add these features wherever practical:

* Search students instantly
* Sort attendance by date/time
* QR code download/print option
* Student profile page
* Teacher profile page
* Attendance correction with audit information
* Session start/end time
* Automatic timestamps
* Confirmation before deleting students
* Loading states and error handling
* Empty states when there is no attendance data
* Demo/sample data for testing

### 15. Security

Do not store sensitive information inside the QR code itself.

The QR should contain only a unique student identifier/token, and the backend should use that identifier to retrieve the student's data.

Validate every attendance request on the server.

Make sure students cannot manually change their attendance status from the frontend.

### Final Requirement

Build this as a **fully functional application**, not just a UI prototype.

Make the database, authentication, QR generation, QR scanning, attendance logic, dashboards, attendance history, duplicate protection, and reports work together end-to-end.

The final result should be polished enough to demonstrate as a **college Smart Attendance System project**.
